# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv
.pytest_cache/

# TLS material — never commit private keys or certs (S1/R17).
# Generate a per-host pair instead; see the operator guide, "HTTPS Setup".
*.pem
*.crt
*.key

# Trajectory logs and run artifacts (R22)
*.jsonl
rlm_repl_*/
docs/*.pdf
k4-acceptance-run.txt
k4_prog3_candidate.txt
logs/k4-gepa-checkpoints/
logs/trajectories/

# Sandbox temp roots. `.tmp_*` is the convention for scratch work whenever a
# root cannot be cleaned up in-session (the sandbox forbids deleting some
# modes); the validation docs have referred to this rule since 2026-09-10.
# The pattern covers *files* as well as directories, because a one-off commit
# message written to `.tmp_msg.txt` was staged by `git add -A` once and shipped.
.tmp_*
.tmp_pytest/
.tmp_rt/

# Permission-probe roots: a directory created with a restrictive mode that this
# session cannot delete (the environment's ACL broker denies the child — see
# AGENTS.md §3), which `git status` therefore reports as an unreadable directory
# rather than an untracked one. Ignored so it stops polluting the tree; remove it
# by hand from an elevated shell.
rt_*/
